==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|taka|lang=non}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈtʰaːka/|lang=is}}
*: {{audio|Taka.ogg|audio}}
*: {{rhymes|aːka|lang=is}}

===Verb===
{{is-verb-strong|tók|tókum|tekið}}

# to [[take]], to [[purloin]] (an object)
#: ''Ég ætla að '''taka''' bílinn.''
#:: I'm going to '''take''' the car.
#: ''Hún var að fara að '''taka''' veskið þitt!''
#:: She was about to '''take''' your purse!
# to [[take]] (time, measure)
#: ''Viltu að ég '''taki''' tímann?''
#:: Do you want me to '''take''' the time?

====Derived terms====
* [[endurtaka]]
* [[margendurtaka]]
* [[taka þátt]]
* [[taka til]]
* [[taka upp]] (to record)
*: ''Ég ætla að '''taka''' þáttinn upp.''
*:: I’m going to '''record''' the show.

